摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Hermes Tool Repair Skill - deterministic tool call repair for LLM agents. Catches common JSON formatting mistakes open models make and fixes them before dispatch, with repair notes that teach the model to self-correct.","id":"gh:1281980482","install_available":false,"language":"Python","name":"tool-repair-skill-for-hermes-and-opencode","slug":"bojansandhaus/tool-repair-skill-for-hermes-and-opencode","topics":["agent-harness","bash","claude-code","cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","hermes","hermes-agent","json","json-repair","llm","opencode","python","self-correction","tool-calling","tool-repair","typescript"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Hermes Tool Repair Skill - deterministic tool call repair for LLM agents. Catches common JSON format"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ting mistakes open models make and fixes them before dispatch, with repair notes that teach the mode"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" models make and fixes them before dispatch, with repair notes that teach the model to self-correct."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# Tool Repair Skill for Hermes and OpenCode"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A **harness-level** fix for LLM tool calling. Catches the common JSON\nformatting mistakes open model"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"s make and fixes them deterministically before\nthe tool executor ever sees them. Ships with adapters"},{"id":"p3s3","text":" for four agent\nframeworks:"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"| Adapter | Language | Repair strategy |"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"| **Hermes** (two calls) | Python | Mutate args pre-dispatch, then append repair notes to the result"},{"id":"p5s2","text":". Built and tested against this library's own 34-test Python suite and 21-test TypeScript parity sui"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"te. |\n| **OpenCode** (plugin) | TypeScript | `tool.execute.before` hook, mutates args directly |\n| *"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"*Claude Code** (hooks) | Bash + jq | `PreToolUse` block so the model retries, `PostToolUse` telemetr"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"y. **Cannot mutate arguments**: PreToolUse can only allow or block, so this adapter corrects by feed"},{"id":"p5s6","text":"back, not in place. |\n| **DeepSeek Harness** (hook bridge) | Bash + jq | `PreToolUse` command hook r"},{"id":"p5s7","text":"egistered with a harness bridge plugin. Also cannot mutate arguments: the seam allows deny, not rewr"},{"id":"p5s8","text":"red with a harness bridge plugin. Also cannot mutate arguments: the seam allows deny, not rewrite. |"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Based on the approach that made DeepSeek V4 Pro outperform Opus 4.7 on tool\ncalling (see CommandCode"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"'s write-up on tool call repairs,\ntheir deep dive,\nand this video walkthrough)."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## The Problem"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Open models (DeepSeek, GLM, Qwen, Kimi) make the same tiny JSON mistakes in tool calls over and over"},{"id":"p8s2","text":". Each mistake triggers a validation error. The model retries with the same bad format. The session "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"degrades through 50+ wasted retry cycles. The model never learns because the error messages are opaq"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"rades through 50+ wasted retry cycles. The model never learns because the error messages are opaque."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"These mistakes are not random. They are a small finite set of patterns caused by the model's trainin"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"g distribution leaking through the tool boundary."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"### Harness vs Model"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Most people frame this as a model problem: \"DeepSeek is bad at tool calling, wait for the next versi"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"on.\" That is wrong. It is a **harness** problem. The harness sits between the model and the tool exe"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"cutor. It decides what to do with the model's output: reject it and waste tokens retrying, or fix it"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" silently and move on. A harness that repairs deterministically turns a bad-at-tool-calling model in"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"to a functional one in about 200 lines of code."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The model did not change. The harness got more forgiving in exactly the places it needed to be."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## The Repair Rules This Applies"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Pattern | What the model sends | What it should be |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| Null omission | `{\"cmd\": \"ls\", \"timeout\": null}` | `{\"cmd\": \"ls\"}` |\n| Null preserved | `{\"name\": "},{"id":"p15s2","text":"null}` where `name` is `required` | unchanged, so the validator reports it |\n| Stringified array | `"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"{\"files\": \"[\\\"a\\\",\\\"b\\\"]\"}` | `{\"files\": [\"a\", \"b\"]}` |\n| Empty object | `{\"files\": {}}` | `{\"files\""},{"id":"p15s4","text":": []}` |\n| Bare string | `{\"files\": \"main.ts\"}` | `{\"files\": [\"main.ts\"]}` |\n| Markdown autolink | `"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"{\"filePath\": \"/x/f.md\"}` | `{\"filePath\": \"/x/f.md\"}` |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## How It Works"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Everything inside the HARNESS BOUNDARY box is your agent framework. The model provides the raw JSON "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"and receives the result. All repair logic, validation, and correction notes are handled at the harne"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"ves the result. All repair logic, validation, and correction notes are handled at the harness layer."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**Key design rule:** a repair only fires when it is unambiguously the right thing, so legitimate dat"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"a survives. The rules that could touch arbitrary content are narrow on purpose. A string is only par"},{"id":"p19s3","text":"sed as an array when it parses as one; an auto-link is only unwrapped when the link text equals the "},{"id":"p19s4","text":"URL's own path component; an array-shaped repair only fires when the schema says the field is an arr"},{"id":"p19s5","text":"ay; a null is only dropped when the schema neither requires the field nor admits null for it. So `wr"},{"id":"p19s6","text":"iteFile` content that happens to be JSON-shaped, a real `click` link, and bracketed prose like `[1, "},{"id":"p19s7","text":"2] and [3, 4]` all pass through untouched, and the test suite asserts each of those cases."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"## Components"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"### `tool_repair.py` (the core library)"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Standalone Python module with no dependencies beyond stdlib. Main entry point:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Can be imported and used by any agent framework, not just Hermes."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### Hermes Agent integration (two calls)"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"The library is built and tested: 34 Python tests, 21 TypeScript parity tests, and\nCI runs both plus "},{"id":"p26s2","text":"the module self-test. Integrating it into a Hermes harness is\ntwo calls at the harness layer, betwee"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"n the model's output and the tool\nexecutor:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"1. **`agent/agent_runtime_helpers.py`**. `sanitize_tool_call_arguments()` is a harness function that"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" walks tool calls before dispatch. Call `repair_function_args()` on the parsed dict after `json.load"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"s()` has already succeeded. If repairs trigger, write the fixed JSON back to the call's arguments."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"2. **`agent/tool_dispatch_helpers.py`**. `make_tool_result_message()` is a harness function that bui"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"lds the tool result before it goes back to the model. Call `deduplicate_repair_notes()` there to app"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"end the repair notes to the result content."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The model reads the repair note alongside the successful result and adapts on the next turn. The har"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"ness did the fixing. The model just benefits from seeing what was fixed."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"### Hermes plugin manifest"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"`references/plugin.yaml` declares the hook surface (`transform_llm_output`) and `plugin-architecture"},{"id":"p31s2","text":".md` sketches the wiring. The `pre_tool_call` hook today can block a call but cannot modify argument"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"s, so the two-call integration above is what you write; `plugin-architecture.md` describes the hook "},{"id":"p31s4","text":"surface that would make it a config toggle instead."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Adapted For Other Frameworks"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"This repo ships adapters for two other agent frameworks in the `adapters/`\ndirectory. Each adapter w"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"raps the same core `tool_repair.py` library with the\nharness-specific wiring."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| Adapter | Location | Key mechanism |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Hermes | `SKILL.md` | `sanitize_tool_call_arguments` pre-dispatch + repair notes. |\n[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
